{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793205852,"nonce":"wlRXb36PHP+amWW8Km4I0pvtqGw=","title":"Preserve class metadata mutations and DCE cast reflection thunks","message":"Ashui 0.2.0 IconSet.build calls Context.getLocalClass().get().meta.add(\":dce\", [], pos). The build context returned a class stub without MetaAccess, so the real Remix catalog failed with cannot call method 'add' on Null. Expose the declaration-backed class view during build macros, retain metadata additions/removals in the shared macro state, and apply them to the built class.\n\nA reducer that adds :dce in a build macro also exposed a separate DCE gap: reflection getter function pointers pass through ABI casts before haxe_register_static_field. The registration scanner did not recognize those exclusively owned cast operands and retained unused getter bodies and SVG payloads. Follow single-use casts when collecting registration operands, preserving all references for live classes and removing the cast chain for dead classes.\n\nRegression checks cover metadata mutations observed through old and fresh class views, missing versus explicit null property initializers, live/dead vtable registrations with cast pointers, and an unused icon payload absent from both serialized BLADE bundles and validated WASM.","files":null}]}